  "label": "intended audience",
  "description": "The meme is designed to target and provoke individuals who hold Islamophobic or misogynistic views, particularly those who may be inclined to believe or spread stereotypes about Muslim communities being untruthful or unreporting of sexual violence. The visual of a crowd of men in traditional Islamic attire, combined with the text 'goats can't talk' and 'why are so few muslim rapes reported?', is crafted to appeal to audiences who are already predisposed to dehumanize or stereotype Muslim men, often by equating them with animals or implying cultural backwardness. The meme’s intent is to normalize or reinforce these harmful tropes, making it most effective for audiences who consume and share content that perpetuates Islamophobic and misogynistic narratives.",
